  "note": "R2-I6. The internal server serves the RAW GHL workflow row (core/audit-configuration.mjs finalize() pushes `row`, not a projection) and identifies it with `idOf`: `_id` first, `id` second, one level of BSON wrapper unwrapped ($oid/_id/id), String()-coerced, empty string rejected. These scenarios are the identity vocabulary the LIVE account actually emits. Every ledger field below is an INDEPENDENT literal, as in roster-scenarios.json: nothing is derived from the rows served alongside it. Each scenario stays on ONE page so it can be layered onto the `one-page` applied-query and source-route ledger.",
